# 121MB clean copy of DSH's app.asar, kept beside the patch script as the
# patching base and restore source. Deliberately NOT tracked: it is a large
# opaque binary that changes wholesale on every DSH upgrade, so committing it
# would bloat every clone for no readable history. Recreate it with
# `tools/patch_asar.ps1 -Refresh` (after a DSH upgrade) or by uninstalling and
# reinstalling DSH.
tools/app.asar.orig

# Working copies kept while reconstructing a clean base. `_npml_ui_chat` holds an
# unpacked release of the DSH chat bundle fetched with `npm pack`, and
# `_app.asar.live-bak` a snapshot of a patched live asar. Both are scratch: they
# are re-creatable from the published package and the installed app, and
# committing them would put another copy of a 565KB bundle plus a 121MB binary
# into history for no readable gain.
tools/_npm_ui_chat/
tools/_app.asar.live-bak

# npm's lockfile. This fork publishes with pnpm (pnpm-lock.yaml is the tracked
# one), so an npm lockfile must not ride along: two lockfiles disagree about
# how to resolve the same tree, and a dependency added here would be invisible
# to `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Kept on disk because this machine has no
# pnpm, so npm is what actually builds here.
package-lock.json
